course: dictionary
lesson: 7645
title: Progress: moving forward
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Progress has more than one meaning, so the sentence around it tells you which one. It can mean getting better at something over time, as in «She is making good progress in reading.» It can also mean moving forward towards a place, as in «The hikers made slow progress up the hill.»
explain: Progress can also be a doing word, a verb: «She progresses well in maths.» As a noun it is uncountable, so we say «good progress» or «some progress», not «a progress» or «two progresses».
explain: The phrase «in progress» means happening now and not finished yet. «The school play is in progress» tells you the play has started but has not ended. To check your meaning, ask: is someone getting better, moving forward, or is something still going on?
fact: Progress means moving forward or getting better at something over time.
fact: «Make progress», «good progress» and «slow progress» are common phrases in school.
fact: «In progress» means happening now and not finished yet.
fact: «Has made some progress» often means very little progress, so read such phrases carefully.
fact: A progress report shows how well you are doing in your learning.
exercise: «Her reading has made good progress this term.» What does progress mean here? | Moving to a new town | *Getting better over time | Stopping and resting | Losing things
exercise: «The hikers made slow progress up the steep hill.» What does progress mean here? | Sat and ate lunch | Ran down the hill quickly | *Moved forward slowly towards the top | Painted the hill green
exercise: «The school project is still in progress.» What does «in progress» mean? | Given back to the teacher | Cancelled for ever | Finished last week | *Happening now and not finished yet
test: «Many teachers suggest giving a new instrument at least a full term before deciding, and recording yourself shows your progress.» What does progress mean here? | A type of music | The street where you live | A quick sprint across the field | *How much you are improving over time
test: Which sentence uses progress as a verb? | *She is progressing well in her piano lessons | A progress chart hangs on the wall | The school gave a progress prize | Good progress is hard to see
exam: «A chart, jar or app that shows your progress helps you keep going.» Why does a progress chart help? | It stops you from trying | *It shows how far you have come, so you want to keep going | It hides how much you have learned | It is only for teachers
